@* Back/previous chevron. A vector, not a text glyph: U+2190 and friends are drawn on the math axis, so they
   render visibly high in a centered box by an amount that shifts with whichever font the head falls back to. *@
<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="@Size" height="@Size" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
     stroke-width="2.25" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
    @* Spans x 8.5–15.5, y 5–19 — symmetric about the viewBox centre, so the ink centres in a round button
       with no nudge. The common "M15 5l-7 7 7 7" form sits half a unit left. *@
    <path d="M15.5 5l-7 7 7 7" />
</svg>
